Title: How to style components using makeStyles and still have lifecycle methods in Material UI?.
Body: <p>I get the below error whenever I try to use <code>makeStyles()</code> with a component with lifecycle methods:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Invalid hook call. Hooks can only be called inside of the body of a function component. This could happen for one of the following reasons:</p>

  <ol>
  <li>You might have mismatching versions of React and the renderer (such as React DOM)</li>
  <li>You might be breaking the Rules of Hooks</li>
  <li>You might have more than one copy of React in the same app</li>
  </ol>
</blockquote>

