<p>slf4j doesn't have a generic <code>log()</code> method that I can find. Does that mean there's no way to implement the above?</p>
<p><strong>Update:</strong> As of SLF4J version 2.0, it is possible to use the <code>Logger.atLevel()</code> method. For example:</p>
<pre><code>import org.slf4j.event.Level;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
...
Logger logger = ... // some slf4j logger of choice
logger.atLevel(Level.Info).log(&quot;hello world&quot;);
</code></pre>

